      "severity": "P1",
      "id": "KUFO_EXTERNAL_DUSTING_TOKEN_LIVENESS",
      "detail": "KUFO processes at most 64 lineage lots per transfer and bounded balance query. Arbitrary holders can create many tiny lots for a victim, after which a full-balance transfer or claimable-decay query can revert with LotTraversalLimit. Manual chunking may recover value but does not eliminate externally triggerable token-liveness degradation."
    },
    {
      "severity": "P1",
      "id": "CALLER_SELECTED_CODE_IDENTITY",
      "detail": "The Furnace constructor accepts addresses and their expected code hashes from the deployer and compares code to those caller-supplied hashes. A counterfeit self-consistent KAIOS/registry/catalyst topology can satisfy the checks without a canonical manifest, deployment receipt, governance authorization or frozen production bank."
    },
    {
      "severity": "P1",
      "id": "UNAUTHORIZED_PROGRAM_LIFE_APPOINTMENTS",
      "detail": "The manifest and contracts encode HUMAN_APPOINTED identities and named successor Program Lives, but current main contains no canonical birth, consent, controller, appointment, revocation or embodiment authority for those records. They remain proposal metadata only."
    },
    {
      "severity": "P1",
      "id": "REAL_ASSET_AND_CHAIN_EFFECTS",
      "detail": "The candidate Furnace transfers real KGEN to a bank, burns real KAIOS and mints KUFO. Even though these operations are transaction-atomic, they are protected asset effects and remain undeployed and unauthorized."
    },
    {
      "severity": "P1",
      "id": "PROTECTED_CURRENT_AND_CANON_OVERWRITE",
      "detail": "The 760-commit-stale branch modifies protected CURRENT, Canon, handbook, scale and verifier surfaces. Two files are three-way diverged and the remaining candidate paths would still overwrite a much newer main lineage."
    },
    {
      "severity": "P1",
      "id": "REGISTRY_BOOTSTRAP_AND_GOVERNANCE_CENTRALIZATION",
      "detail": "A single owner can replace organs immediately while bootstrapOpen and later uses a one-hour minimum delay without quorum, controller acceptance, recovery, conflict separation or canonical deployment authority."
    },
    {
      "severity": "P1",
      "id": "HISTORICAL_EXTERNAL_EVIDENCE_NOT_CURRENT_AUTHORITY",
      "detail": "Stored BSC/fork and Mainnet-compatibility reports are August observations. They do not prove current chain state, signer/controller authority, deployment authorization or custody; the optional verifier can read a caller-configured RPC but is not run by the exact-head workflow."
    },
    {
      "severity": "P1",
      "id": "SCALE_AND_DEPENDENCY_CONFLICT",
